# {{axisStudlyPlural}}

The {{axisPlural}} {{humanName}} ships, how to name one in an icon path, and when to reach for each.

{{humanName}} ships the following {{axisPlural}}. Reference any icon as `{{packageName}}::<{{axis}}>/<icon-name>` (or just `<icon-name>` for the default {{axis}}).

| {{axisStudly}} | Path prefix | Style |
|---|---|---|
| `default` | `<name>` (no prefix needed) | <!-- describe the default {{axis}} --> |
| <!-- add rows for additional {{axisPlural}} --> | | |

## Examples

```blade
{{-- Default {{axis}} --}}
<x-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::home" class="w-6 h-6" />

{{-- Explicit {{axis}} path --}}
<x-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::default/home" class="w-6 h-6" />
```

Fluent helper:

```blade
{{ ichava('{{packageName}}::home')->color('#4338ca')->class('w-6 h-6') }}
```

## {{axisStudly}} enum (PHP)

```php
use {{namespace}}\Enums\{{axisStudly}};

{{axisStudly}}::DEFAULT->value;            // 'default'
{{axisStudly}}::DEFAULT->isDefault();      // true
{{axisStudly}}::default();                 // {{axisStudly}}::DEFAULT
```

The enum implements `IconSetVariantInterface` from core, so it works wherever core's registry expects a {{axis}}.

